# Everything the build context does not need. Keeping this tight matters more
# than it looks: the context is uploaded to the builder on every build, and a
# stray .git or node_modules turns a sub-second transfer into a slow one — and on
# a shared builder, a leaked .git also hands the build any credentials stored in
# it.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore

# Docs and licences: the image carries its provenance in OCI labels instead.
*.md
LICENSE

# Local tool state and editor droppings.
.bin
.cache
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
.mise.toml
mise.toml

# Build and test output. Any binary here was built for the host, not for
# $TARGETPLATFORM, so letting one into the context risks shipping the wrong one.
/bin
/dist
/out
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile

# Compose and chart definitions consume the image; they are not inputs to it.
compose.yaml
compose.yml
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.yml
/chart
